title the comment that moved into the meter -- a standfast on my own round, booked as %314 and closed
prompt Continuing the same seat. The %304 round had landed and pushed to both remotes; reading the ASCII ratchet it had named as a next lap found that ratchet standing over its ceiling.
think The mechanism, plainly: tools/fixtures/rye_comment_ascii_scan.sh counts non-ASCII on lines whose first non-blank characters are // and deliberately excludes a trailing comment after code, because finding one needs to know whether the // sits inside a string. My split pass lifted twenty trailing comments onto their own lines, three of them carrying an em-dash, so three characters crossed from the unread side of that boundary to the read side. RYE_COMMENT_ASCII read 4341 against a ceiling of 4338 on a tree already on both remotes.
think The check I DID run was honest and useless: git diff | grep '^+' | grep -c over a non-ASCII class, which read zero for every touched file. That was true. The characters were not added, they were relocated, and a diff of added lines cannot tell those apart. The lesson generalizes past ASCII -- a meter with an honest exclusion has a boundary, and reformatting is content-neutral only where no meter's scope is drawn by position. The scan says so in its own header, this therefore UNDERCOUNTS on purpose, and an undercount is a promise about what goes unread.
think Repaired by subtraction and one turn of the ratchet: three em-dashes to --, and five typographic minus signs standing where arithmetic wanted a hyphen (threshold - 1, qe + qr - n, now - granted) to -, since a lap holding a file open owes the ratchet its turn. constel's comment-line reading fell 49 to 41, the living reading 4341 to 4333, and the ceiling fell to 4333 with an arc line naming why. Left alone: 32 section signs in Raft citations and 7 set-theory marks, which are notation the ASCII table leaves to a reader's judgment.
obs ERRATUM against my own log 20260828.133116, which is committed testimony and therefore corrected here rather than edited. Its second obs reads "My edit left the count unchanged at 276 lines before and after, so nothing was made worse." The measurement was real and the wrong one: 276 counts FILE LINES containing any non-ASCII, and the meter counts CHARACTERS on comment lines. The right reading was 46 to 49. The claim in that log is false and the lap that wrote it is the lap that raised the ratchet.
obs Booked %314 from the anointed spine after a fetch -- reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next read 314 with xy/main equal to HEAD, so no collision. The headline and its span sentence both needed the new N; reds_ledger_monotone_witness refused twice before both moved, which is the guard doing exactly the job REDS %127 seated it for.
obs Still no clean roster reading: the peer holds 33 staged glow/gen/ files, and my own cold run has been alive 27 minutes without finishing. Both commits this round are path-limited around that index.
loom ratchet_before=4341 ceiling_before=4338 over_by=3 ratchet_after=4333 ceiling_after=4333
