recommend check-in (either) -- both commits are on xy and debrided; the open rows left are Pond's %306, Sound's %311, and Keaton's gated %291/%295/%301. The ITINERARY Prior-laps row and git nib are four laps stale and want the next work commit that touches the card, rather than a pin-only follow-up the tidy rule refuses.
